1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,056
Welcome to Unit Nine of Algebra One:
quadratic functions and equations.

2
00:00:05,506 --> 00:00:09,197
In this lesson, we'll look at the graphs
of quadratic functions.

3
00:00:10,333 --> 00:00:17,166
A quadratic function has the form f of x
equals a x squared plus b x plus c, with a

4
00:00:17,166 --> 00:00:17,907
not zero.

5
00:00:18,357 --> 00:00:24,037
The simplest one is y equals x squared.
Its graph is a U-shaped curve called a

6
00:00:24,037 --> 00:00:24,693
parabola.

7
00:00:25,833 --> 00:00:31,477
The turning point of a parabola is the
vertex. For y equals x squared, it's the

8
00:00:31,477 --> 00:00:31,977
origin.

9
00:00:32,427 --> 00:00:37,646
The parabola is symmetric about a vertical
line through the vertex, called the axis

10
00:00:37,646 --> 00:00:38,401
of symmetry.

11
00:00:39,533 --> 00:00:44,056
When a is positive, the parabola opens up,
and the vertex is a minimum.

12
00:00:44,506 --> 00:00:50,049
When a is negative, it opens down, and the
vertex is a maximum. The bigger the size

13
00:00:50,049 --> 00:00:52,186
of a, the narrower the parabola.

14
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:57,643
The axis of symmetry is x equals negative
b over two a.

15
00:00:58,093 --> 00:01:04,024
For y equals x squared minus four x plus
three, that's four over two, which is two.

16
00:01:04,024 --> 00:01:09,599
Plug in two: four minus eight plus three
is negative one. So the vertex is two

17
00:01:09,599 --> 00:01:10,957
comma negative one.

18
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:16,751
Now graph it. Plot the vertex, then the y
intercept, zero comma three.

19
00:01:17,201 --> 00:01:22,391
By symmetry, four comma three is also on
the graph. Connect them with a smooth

20
00:01:22,391 --> 00:01:22,790
curve.

21
00:01:23,933 --> 00:01:29,288
Your turn. Find the vertex of y equals x
squared plus six x plus five.

22
00:01:29,738 --> 00:01:31,274
Pause the video and try it.

23
00:01:31,724 --> 00:01:37,420
x equals negative six over two, which is
negative three. Then y is nine minus

24
00:01:37,420 --> 00:01:43,190
eighteen plus five, which is negative
four. The vertex is negative three comma

25
00:01:43,190 --> 00:01:44,225
negative four.

26
00:01:45,366 --> 00:01:50,654
In this lesson, we'll write parabolas in
vertex form, which shows the vertex right

27
00:01:50,654 --> 00:01:50,977
away.

28
00:01:52,099 --> 00:01:57,881
Vertex form is y equals a times the
quantity x minus h, squared, plus k.

29
00:01:58,331 --> 00:02:00,165
The vertex is h comma k.

30
00:02:01,299 --> 00:02:03,454
The h shifts the graph left or right.

31
00:02:03,904 --> 00:02:10,087
y equals x minus three, squared, moves y
equals x squared three units right. Watch

32
00:02:10,087 --> 00:02:12,651
the sign: minus three means right.

33
00:02:13,799 --> 00:02:15,847
The k shifts the graph up or down.

34
00:02:16,297 --> 00:02:19,305
y equals x squared plus two moves it up
two.

35
00:02:20,433 --> 00:02:22,267
The a stretches or reflects it.

36
00:02:22,717 --> 00:02:28,756
y equals two x squared is narrower. y
equals negative x squared flips it upside

37
00:02:28,756 --> 00:02:29,139
down.

38
00:02:30,266 --> 00:02:35,130
Graph y equals negative the quantity x
plus one, squared, plus four.

39
00:02:35,580 --> 00:02:39,527
The vertex is negative one comma four, and
it opens down.

40
00:02:40,666 --> 00:02:46,383
Your turn. What is the vertex of y equals
two times the quantity x minus five,

41
00:02:46,383 --> 00:02:49,754
squared, minus three? Does it open up or
down?

42
00:02:50,204 --> 00:02:51,740
Pause the video and try it.

43
00:02:52,190 --> 00:02:56,947
The vertex is five comma negative three,
and since a is two, it opens up.

44
00:02:58,066 --> 00:03:03,277
Now we start solving quadratic equations.
In this lesson, we'll use graphs and

45
00:03:03,277 --> 00:03:04,146
square roots.

46
00:03:05,266 --> 00:03:11,625
The solutions of a x squared plus b x plus
c equals zero are the x intercepts of the

47
00:03:11,625 --> 00:03:12,306
parabola.

48
00:03:12,756 --> 00:03:18,531
They're also called roots or zeros. For y
equals x squared minus four, the graph

49
00:03:18,531 --> 00:03:20,841
crosses at negative two and two.

50
00:03:21,966 --> 00:03:26,339
A parabola can cross the x axis twice,
touch it once, or miss it.

51
00:03:26,789 --> 00:03:31,099
So a quadratic equation has two, one, or
no real solutions.

52
00:03:32,233 --> 00:03:36,777
When there's no x term, use square roots.
x squared equals twenty-five.

53
00:03:37,227 --> 00:03:41,643
x can be five, or negative five. Don't
forget the negative root.

54
00:03:42,766 --> 00:03:46,179
Solve three x squared minus forty-eight
equals zero.

55
00:03:46,629 --> 00:03:52,367
Add forty-eight: three x squared equals
forty-eight. Divide by three: x squared

56
00:03:52,367 --> 00:03:55,781
equals sixteen. So x equals plus or minus
four.

57
00:03:56,899 --> 00:04:00,398
Solve the quantity x minus two, squared,
equals nine.

58
00:04:00,848 --> 00:04:07,332
Take square roots: x minus two equals plus
or minus three. So x equals five, or x

59
00:04:07,332 --> 00:04:08,933
equals negative one.

60
00:04:09,066 --> 00:04:13,437
Your turn. Solve two x squared equals
seventy-two.

61
00:04:13,887 --> 00:04:15,423
Pause the video and try it.

62
00:04:15,873 --> 00:04:20,225
x squared equals thirty-six, so x equals
plus or minus six.

63
00:04:21,366 --> 00:04:26,708
In Unit Eight we learned to factor. In
this lesson, we'll use factoring to solve

64
00:04:26,708 --> 00:04:28,043
quadratic equations.

65
00:04:29,166 --> 00:04:34,980
The zero product property: if a times b
equals zero, then a equals zero, or b

66
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:35,886
equals zero.

67
00:04:36,336 --> 00:04:38,640
It only works with zero on one side.

68
00:04:39,766 --> 00:04:45,185
Solve the quantity x minus three, times
the quantity x plus five, equals zero.

69
00:04:45,635 --> 00:04:52,346
Either x minus three is zero, so x equals
three, or x plus five is zero, so x equals

70
00:04:52,346 --> 00:04:53,464
negative five.

71
00:04:54,599 --> 00:04:58,013
Solve x squared plus x minus twelve equals
zero.

72
00:04:58,463 --> 00:05:04,873
Factor: x plus four, times x minus three.
So x equals negative four, or x equals

73
00:05:04,873 --> 00:05:05,353
three.

74
00:05:06,499 --> 00:05:08,654
Solve x squared equals five x.

75
00:05:09,104 --> 00:05:15,648
First get zero on one side: x squared
minus five x equals zero. Factor out x: x

76
00:05:15,648 --> 00:05:18,299
times the quantity x minus five.

77
00:05:18,749 --> 00:05:24,551
So x equals zero or five. Don't divide by
x, or you'll lose the zero solution.

78
00:05:25,699 --> 00:05:29,625
Solve two x squared plus seven x plus
three equals zero.

79
00:05:30,075 --> 00:05:36,669
It factors as two x plus one, times x plus
three. So x equals negative one half, or

80
00:05:36,669 --> 00:05:37,861
negative three.

81
00:05:38,999 --> 00:05:43,629
Your turn. Solve x squared minus seven x
plus ten equals zero.

82
00:05:44,079 --> 00:05:45,615
Pause the video and try it.

83
00:05:46,065 --> 00:05:51,931
It factors as x minus two, times x minus
five. So x equals two or five.

84
00:05:53,066 --> 00:05:57,957
Not every quadratic factors nicely.
Completing the square works on any

85
00:05:57,957 --> 00:05:58,655
quadratic.

86
00:05:59,799 --> 00:06:05,175
x squared plus six x plus nine is a
perfect square: x plus three, squared.

87
00:06:05,625 --> 00:06:10,916
The nine comes from half of six, squared.
Half of b, squared, completes the square.

88
00:06:11,066 --> 00:06:15,095
Here are the steps. Move the constant to
the right side.

89
00:06:15,545 --> 00:06:20,879
Add half of b, squared, to both sides.
Then write the left side as a square and

90
00:06:20,879 --> 00:06:22,095
take square roots.

91
00:06:23,233 --> 00:06:26,923
Solve x squared plus six x minus seven
equals zero.

92
00:06:27,373 --> 00:06:33,062
Move the seven: x squared plus six x
equals seven. Add nine to both sides: x

93
00:06:33,062 --> 00:06:35,757
plus three, squared, equals sixteen.

94
00:06:36,207 --> 00:06:43,162
So x plus three equals plus or minus four.
x equals one, or x equals negative seven.

95
00:06:44,299 --> 00:06:47,798
When b is odd, you get fractions, but the
steps are the same.

96
00:06:48,248 --> 00:06:53,432
For x squared plus three x, half of three
is three halves, and its square is nine

97
00:06:53,432 --> 00:06:53,944
fourths.

98
00:06:54,066 --> 00:06:57,925
Completing the square also gives vertex
form.

99
00:06:58,375 --> 00:07:04,504
x squared minus four x plus one equals x
minus two, squared, minus three. So the

100
00:07:04,504 --> 00:07:07,185
vertex is two comma negative three.

101
00:07:08,333 --> 00:07:13,957
Your turn. Solve x squared plus four x
minus five equals zero by completing the

102
00:07:13,957 --> 00:07:14,455
square.

103
00:07:14,905 --> 00:07:16,441
Pause the video and try it.

104
00:07:16,891 --> 00:07:23,648
x squared plus four x equals five. Add
four: x plus two, squared, equals nine. So

105
00:07:23,648 --> 00:07:26,150
x equals one or negative five.

106
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:32,225
Completing the square on a general
quadratic gives a formula that solves

107
00:07:32,225 --> 00:07:33,935
every quadratic equation.

108
00:07:35,067 --> 00:07:41,420
For a x squared plus b x plus c equals
zero, x equals negative b, plus or minus

109
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:46,245
the square root of b squared minus four a
c, all over two a.

110
00:07:46,695 --> 00:07:48,146
It's worth memorizing.

111
00:07:49,267 --> 00:07:53,789
First, write the equation in standard
form, and read off a, b and c.

112
00:07:54,239 --> 00:08:00,523
For two x squared minus three x equals
two, subtract two: a is two, b is negative

113
00:08:00,523 --> 00:08:02,773
three, and c is negative two.

114
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:09,463
Plug in. b squared minus four a c is nine
plus sixteen, which is twenty-five, and

115
00:08:09,463 --> 00:08:11,111
its square root is five.

116
00:08:11,561 --> 00:08:17,619
So x equals three plus or minus five, over
four. That's two, or negative one half.

117
00:08:18,767 --> 00:08:20,985
The answers aren't always whole numbers.

118
00:08:21,435 --> 00:08:27,780
For x squared plus two x minus one equals
zero, x equals negative one plus or minus

119
00:08:27,780 --> 00:08:33,972
the square root of two. Leave it exact, or
round to about zero point four one and

120
00:08:33,972 --> 00:08:36,113
negative two point four one.

121
00:08:37,233 --> 00:08:42,796
Which method to use? If there's no x term,
use square roots. If it factors easily,

122
00:08:42,796 --> 00:08:43,271
factor.

123
00:08:43,721 --> 00:08:47,283
Otherwise, use the quadratic formula. It
always works.

124
00:08:48,433 --> 00:08:54,297
Your turn. Solve x squared minus four x
minus five equals zero with the quadratic

125
00:08:54,297 --> 00:08:54,876
formula.

126
00:08:55,326 --> 00:08:56,862
Pause the video and try it.

127
00:08:57,312 --> 00:09:04,144
b squared minus four a c is sixteen plus
twenty, which is thirty-six. x equals four

128
00:09:04,144 --> 00:09:08,341
plus or minus six, over two: five, or
negative one.

129
00:09:09,466 --> 00:09:14,088
The part under the square root in the
quadratic formula tells you how many

130
00:09:14,088 --> 00:09:16,399
solutions there are, without solving.

131
00:09:17,533 --> 00:09:20,754
b squared minus four a c is called the
discriminant.

132
00:09:21,204 --> 00:09:24,020
It decides whether the square root is a
real number.

133
00:09:25,166 --> 00:09:29,027
If the discriminant is positive, there are
two real solutions.

134
00:09:29,477 --> 00:09:35,469
For x squared minus five x plus six, it's
twenty-five minus twenty-four, which is

135
00:09:35,469 --> 00:09:39,760
one. Two solutions. The parabola crosses
the x axis twice.

136
00:09:40,899 --> 00:09:43,566
If it's zero, there's exactly one
solution.

137
00:09:44,016 --> 00:09:49,864
For x squared minus six x plus nine, it's
thirty-six minus thirty-six, which is

138
00:09:49,864 --> 00:09:53,936
zero. The parabola just touches the axis
at its vertex.

139
00:09:55,066 --> 00:09:57,818
If it's negative, there are no real
solutions.

140
00:09:58,268 --> 00:10:04,131
For x squared plus x plus three, it's one
minus twelve, which is negative eleven.

141
00:10:04,131 --> 00:10:06,375
The parabola misses the x axis.

142
00:10:07,499 --> 00:10:10,273
The discriminant is a quick check before
you solve.

143
00:10:10,723 --> 00:10:15,875
If it's a perfect square, like one or
twenty-five, the quadratic also factors

144
00:10:15,875 --> 00:10:17,080
over the integers.

145
00:10:18,199 --> 00:10:24,113
Your turn. How many real solutions does
two x squared plus four x plus five equals

146
00:10:24,113 --> 00:10:24,834
zero have?

147
00:10:25,284 --> 00:10:26,820
Pause the video and try it.

148
00:10:27,270 --> 00:10:32,373
Sixteen minus forty is negative
twenty-four. It's negative, so there are

149
00:10:32,373 --> 00:10:33,649
no real solutions.

150
00:10:34,766 --> 00:10:40,177
Quadratics describe real motion and
shapes. In this last lesson of Unit Nine,

151
00:10:40,177 --> 00:10:41,934
we'll use them as models.

152
00:10:43,066 --> 00:10:49,270
A ball is thrown upward. Its height in
feet after t seconds is h equals negative

153
00:10:49,270 --> 00:10:52,837
sixteen t squared plus sixty-four t plus
five.

154
00:10:53,287 --> 00:10:57,233
The negative leading coefficient makes the
parabola open down.

155
00:10:58,366 --> 00:11:03,744
The highest point is the vertex. t equals
negative sixty-four over negative

156
00:11:03,744 --> 00:11:06,110
thirty-two, which is two seconds.

157
00:11:06,560 --> 00:11:12,243
h of two is negative sixty-four plus one
hundred twenty-eight plus five, which is

158
00:11:12,243 --> 00:11:13,365
sixty-nine feet.

159
00:11:14,499 --> 00:11:20,265
The ball lands when h equals zero. Use the
quadratic formula, and keep only the

160
00:11:20,265 --> 00:11:21,433
positive answer.

161
00:11:21,883 --> 00:11:24,528
t is about four point zero eight seconds.

162
00:11:25,666 --> 00:11:30,544
A rectangle has a length three more than
its width, and an area of forty square

163
00:11:30,544 --> 00:11:30,914
units.

164
00:11:31,364 --> 00:11:37,813
w times the quantity w plus three equals
forty. So w squared plus three w minus

165
00:11:37,813 --> 00:11:44,506
forty equals zero, which factors as w plus
eight, times w minus five. The width is

166
00:11:44,506 --> 00:11:46,873
five and the length is eight.

167
00:11:47,999 --> 00:11:51,626
To identify a model from a table, look at
the differences.

168
00:11:52,076 --> 00:11:57,307
Constant first differences: linear.
Constant second differences: quadratic.

169
00:11:57,307 --> 00:11:59,329
Constant ratios: exponential.

170
00:12:00,466 --> 00:12:06,475
Your turn. A ball's height is h equals
negative sixteen t squared plus thirty-two

171
00:12:06,475 --> 00:12:08,701
t. What is its maximum height?

172
00:12:09,151 --> 00:12:10,687
Pause the video and try it.

173
00:12:11,137 --> 00:12:17,650
The vertex is at t equals one. h of one is
negative sixteen plus thirty-two, which is

174
00:12:17,650 --> 00:12:18,646
sixteen feet.

175
00:12:18,766 --> 00:12:24,971
That completes Unit Nine. Next, we'll
finish the course with Unit Ten: radicals

176
00:12:24,971 --> 00:12:29,847
and data. If this helped, subscribe to
School Math, Explained, and turn on

177
00:12:29,847 --> 00:12:33,142
notifications so you don't miss it. See
you there.

